# No leftover temp files after features

## Mandate

When a server/WZ-tool/feature batch finishes, **delete** temporary and process artifacts. Do not keep `_tmp*`, probe JSON, compile logs, or `_batch_commit_*.py` after use.

## Delete (examples)

- `_tmp*`, `_boot_test/`, `_cmp*`, `_batch_commit_server.py` (after commits)
- `*.log`, `*.err`, `tmp_*.txt`, `logs_server_*.log`
- Tool build trees: `tools/**/bin`, `obj`, `out`, `__pycache__`, `*.bak_work`, one-off `ProbeSkill.csx` / `Verify.csx`
- Downloaded binaries not meant for git (e.g. `tools/handle64.exe`)

## Keep

- Real Java/TS sources, Flyway, scripts under `scripts/`
- Intentional `tools/*.py` utilities and small extract project sources (not their build outputs)
- `.cursor/rules` and docs the team relies on

## After cleanup

Update `.gitignore` if a new junk pattern appeared. Prefer deleting untracked junk over committing it.
